// Shadowfetch Fireproof: APT periodic policy.
//
// THE ONLY APT::Periodic DECLARATION IN THE PRODUCT (Stage U).
// shadowfetch-defaults used to ship 52shadowfetch-unattended.conf, which set
// Unattended-Upgrade "1" and Remove-Unused-Dependencies "true". Both files
// shipped; which one won was decided by nothing but filename order, and it
// was this one - so the documented behaviour ("auto-apply security updates")
// was never the actual behaviour. Had the other file won, packages would
// have been installed AND REMOVED with no analyze, no approval, no verify
// battery and no recorded Phoenix Point, leaving the rollback record
// describing a different transaction than the one on disk. It was deleted,
// and packages/shadowfetch-fireproof/tests/test_single_update_authority.py
// fails if a second declaration appears anywhere under packages/.
//
// Package LISTS refresh daily so the Fireproof badge and analyze screen
// stay honest without any daemon of ours touching the network. Nothing
// is ever downloaded or installed unattended: downloads happen only in
// Fireproof's labeled, post-consent download phase, and installs only
// after the NEWS gate.
APT::Periodic::Update-Package-Lists "1";
APT::Periodic::Download-Upgradeable-Packages "0";
APT::Periodic::Unattended-Upgrade "0";
APT::Periodic::AutocleanInterval "0";
